From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: factory registrations, creation flags, video memory reservation, device residency/priority/EnqueueSetEvent

The factory's occlusion, stereo and adapters-changed registrations were
E_NOTIMPL stubs; they now validate the event or window, hand out process-wide
unique cookies, and Unregister* drops them (an unknown cookie of the adapters
call is DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL). The hardware content protection teardown
event of the adapter works the same way. GetCreationFlags returns the flags
given to CreateDXGIFactory2, IsCurrent and IsWindowedStereoEnabled answer
without a FIXME, and CreateSoftwareAdapter validates its arguments.

SetVideoMemoryReservation stores the reservation per segment group and
QueryVideoMemoryInfo reports it, capped at what is available.

On the device, Set/GetGPUThreadPriority keep the -7..7 value,
QueryResourceResidency reports resources as resident, OfferResources and
ReclaimResources validate and succeed without discarding, Trim is a no-op, and
EnqueueSetEvent signals the event after the GPU work queued so far has
finished (an event query behind the immediate context).
